# Corpus tier floors. One line per tier, lowest PHP that tier's corpus runs on.
#
# Membership is NOT listed here: scripts/pgo_tiers.py computes it from
# matrix.json -- a version belongs to the tier with the greatest floor <= it.
# The release Composer resolves against, the builder image and the image tag
# are all derived from matrix.json too. This file only answers "where do the
# boundaries fall", and the boundaries are set by what the frameworks support,
# measured rather than assumed:
#
#   8.2  Laravel 12 (php ^8.2), Symfony 7 (php >=8.2), WordPress 7.0.4.
#        Laravel 13 needs 8.3, so 8.2 is where the current line stops.
#   8.1  Laravel 10 (php ^8.1) and Symfony 6.4 (php >=8.1) are the newest that
#        install on 8.1; Laravel 11 and Symfony 7 both require 8.2. WordPress
#        7.0.4 still applies (it wants 7.4).
#   7.2  Laravel 6 (php ^7.2.5), Symfony 5.4 (php >=7.2.5) -- the newest
#        Symfony that runs on PHP 7 at all -- and WordPress 6.9.7, the last
#        line whose $required_php_version (7.2.24) is below PHP 7.2.34.
#        WordPress 7.0 requires 7.4, which is what made the previous 7.4 floor
#        unusable on 7.2 and 7.3.
#   7.1  Laravel 5.8 (php ^7.1.3), Symfony 4.4 (php >=7.1.3) -- the last
#        Symfony below the 7.2.5 floor 5.4 sets -- and WordPress 6.5.5
#        (7.0.0), the last line below WordPress 6.6's 7.2.24, with the 2.1.13
#        SQLite drop-in (php 7.0).
#   7.0  Laravel 5.5 (php >=7.0.0), Symfony 3.4 (php >=7.0.8, the last branch
#        below Symfony 4.4's 7.1.3), same WordPress 6.5.5 and 2.1.13 drop-in.
#        This tier existed only after task 16 fixed the bundled-libsqlite
#        defect: PHP 7.0 used to link php's own libsqlite 3.14.2, and the
#        drop-in writes its type cache with UPSERT, which SQLite grew in 3.24,
#        so WordPress died at CREATE TABLE wp_users. It now links Debian's
#        3.46.1 like every other version -- see php/system-libs.lock, which
#        asserts that per image so this cannot regress unnoticed.
8.2
8.1
7.2
7.1
7.0
